Task: Auto-provision Kibana's purerest-logs Data View (post-review fix)

Summary: User hit this live while interactively exercising the finished
stack (docker compose up + Gatling load test + open Grafana/Kibana) — asked
"I need to configure kibana to see the logs.. not seeing anything." Root
cause: Kibana (unlike Grafana) has no file-based Data View provisioning;
the track's Phase 4 work never created one, so Discover was genuinely
empty despite Filebeat correctly shipping documents into Elasticsearch
(confirmed: 4500+ real docs present via a direct ES query at the time).

Fixed with a one-shot `kibana-setup` compose service (curlimages/curl)
that POSTs the Data View + sets it default via Kibana's own HTTP API,
gated on a new Kibana healthcheck. Verified idempotent (a second run
returns 400 on the already-exists POST but the container still exits 0 and
the default-index call still succeeds). Re-ran scripts/verify-observability-
stack.sh end-to-end with a new assertion added for this Data View: all
checks passed, including the pre-existing metrics/log checks (unaffected).

Files changed: docker-compose.yml, scripts/verify-observability-stack.sh,
conductor/tech-stack.md, README.md

Why: This was a genuine, user-facing gap in the finished track's Phase 4
deliverable (Kibana browsable was an explicit acceptance criterion) that
automated verification didn't catch because the verify script queried
Elasticsearch directly rather than through Kibana's own UI/API — exactly
the kind of gap real interactive use surfaces that a script checking the
wrong layer misses.
